I woke up early this morning.
The sun shone brightly into my bedroom.
I lay in bed and thought about my home in Mexico.
Today is actually my birthday.
I turn thirty-two years old today.
It is my first birthday away from my family.
I felt a little nostalgic about it.
But then I picked up my phone from the nightstand.
My family has sent many loving messages.
They wrote them last night while I slept.
My parents have recorded a funny video with Lola, our dog.
My sister Sofía has written a long and sweet text.
And my brother Diego sent a picture of my favorite cake.
I smiled broadly when I saw the picture.
They have not forgotten my big day at all.
I replied to all the messages immediately.
I wrote to them that I love and miss them.
I am far away from home today.
But I have had a fantastic start to my birthday anyway.
